From e3dc98c01360647482f820ad01782e6d73b3d573 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:00:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] charset: prescan the first 1024 bytes for a meta charset

The HTML standard's prescan of a byte stream reads its first 1024
bytes (it was 512 in early drafts, which Hubbub followed). Many pages
put their meta charset between the two, after long xmlns attributes or
other meta elements. Hubbub's prescan missed it there, so the page was
first read as Windows-1252; the client then has to parse it again when
the tree builder reports the meta, or reads UTF-8 as Windows-1252 if it
doesn't.
---
 src/charset/detect.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/charset/detect.c b/src/charset/detect.c
index d2d6816..8d0823c 100644
--- a/src/charset/detect.c
+++ b/src/charset/detect.c
@@ -216,7 +216,8 @@ uint16_t hubbub_charset_scan_meta(const uint8_t *data, size_t len)
 	if (data == NULL)
 		return 0;
 
-	end = pos + min(512, len);
+	/* The HTML standard's prescan reads the first 1024 bytes */
+	end = pos + min(1024, len);
 
 	/* 1. */
 	while (pos < end) {
-- 
2.43.0

